    "result_text": "The full suite consists of a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`); the other two files are the base harness and a helper. Everything is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the code generator:\n   - `nextCustomerCode` now takes `city` and `lastName`, prepends `CITY3` (upper-cased first 3 letters of city), and computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** sequence \u2014 one more than the number of existing owners in that city (matched case-insensitively) \u2014 instead of the old global count.\n   - Updated the call site in `addOwner` and the method's javadoc.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 no code change needed. `membershipNumber` is formatted as `<customerCode>-M<YY>` directly on top of `customerCode`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `SPR-SMI-0007-M26`). `membershipTier`, `displayName`, and `initials` don't derive from `customerCode`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` description/example and the `membershipNumber` example to match the new format.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` asserts the code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`, which now holds.",
